# Test-run artifacts. The verify-* folders are .gui dumps produced by a patcher
# run at one resolution -- regenerate them rather than storing them (see
# testing/README.md). latest-generated-*-path.txt records an absolute path from
# whichever machine produced them.
testing/virtual-display/verify-*/
testing/virtual-display/latest-generated-*-path.txt

# Vendored third-party driver package. Obtain it from the upstream project and
# verify the SHA-256 recorded in testing/virtual-display/README.md instead.
testing/virtual-display/VDD.Control.*/
testing/virtual-display/VDD.Control.*.zip

# Game-derived build inputs. Kept inside the project so it is self-contained,
# but never committed -- these are BioWare's files. See build-inputs/README.md.
build-inputs/*
!build-inputs/README.md

# Machine-specific build settings (build.local.example.ps1 is the template).
build.local.ps1

# third_party is an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist.
#
# Mods are dropped in here for comparison, and we have no permission to redistribute
# most of them. Two denylists in a row failed: the first was fixed-depth and stopped
# matching when everything moved into Included/, staging ~800 files of other people's
# work; the second listed the mods present at the time and missed the next one added,
# which reached a commit. So everything is ignored by default and each redistributable
# is named explicitly below. A new mod dropped in here is invisible to git until
# someone deliberately un-ignores it.
#
# Note the shape: git will not look inside an excluded directory, so each level has to
# be re-included before the level below it can be excluded.
third_party/*
!third_party/Included/
third_party/Included/*

# KOTOR High Resolution Menus (ndix UR, GPL-3.0) -- the per-resolution GUI layouts
# KMRP derives from and ships. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
!third_party/Included/kotor-high-resolution-menus-1.5/

# K1 Modern Driver Compatibility standalone build (Synchro, MPL-2.0), shipped inside
# the patcher with the author's permission. The negations for the binaries are needed
# because the global *.dll rule above would otherwise drop the proxy DLL from the
# release we distribute. See docs/third-party-driver-compat.md.
!third_party/Included/k1-modern-driver-compatibility-1.2.0 by Synchro/
# K1 Area Map Fixes (Derslok, GPL-3.0). We redistribute ONE file from it: the 250-entry
# map-note correction table, which gold bakes into .kmn. Its licence and the author's
# own technical notes ship with it so the data's provenance travels with the data. His
# compiled patcher and its 32 MB of dependencies are NOT redistributed and stay ignored.
# Bundled Override art, shipped inside the patcher with their authors' permission.
# Only what we actually redistribute: the icon pack's optional BonusICON variants and
# the portraits' duplicate .tpc set are not shipped and stay ignored.
!third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/
third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/*
!third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/ReadMe.txt
!third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/Portraits NPC/
third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/Portraits NPC/*
!third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/Portraits NPC/tga/
!third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/Portraits PLAYER/
third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/Portraits PLAYER/*
!third_party/Included/Party Portraits by MadDerp/Portraits PLAYER/tga/
!third_party/Included/KOTOR1 HD ICON PACK*/
third_party/Included/KOTOR1 HD ICON PACK*/*
!third_party/Included/KOTOR1 HD ICON PACK*/README.txt
!third_party/Included/KOTOR1 HD ICON PACK*/Override/

